# jqscore: Q-score on the GPU with JAX. The jax[cuda13] wheels bring their
# own CUDA libraries, so the host needs only an NVIDIA driver (>= 580 for
# CUDA 13), which apptainer passes in with --nv. Without --nv, or without a
# GPU, JAX runs on the CPU.
#
# Build from the repository root (%files paths are relative to it):
#   apptainer build --fakeroot jqscore.sif container/jqscore.def
# For a driver older than 580, use the CUDA 12 wheels (driver >= 525):
#   apptainer build --fakeroot --build-arg JAX="jax[cuda12]==0.9.2" jqscore.sif container/jqscore.def
# The build ends with the test suite on the CPU (skip it with --notest).
#
# Run (see %help):
#   apptainer run --nv jqscore.sif STRUCTURE MAP [options]
#   apptainer exec --nv jqscore.sif jqscore-cmd CHIMERA map=MAP cif=CIF [cif=CIF ...] [sigma=S]
Bootstrap: docker
From: python:3.12-slim

%arguments
    JAX="jax[cuda13]==0.9.2"

%files
    pyproject.toml /opt/jqscore/pyproject.toml
    README.md /opt/jqscore/README.md
    LICENSE /opt/jqscore/LICENSE
    jqscore /opt/jqscore/jqscore
    tests /opt/jqscore/tests

%labels
    MAINTAINER Arthur Zalevsky <aozalevsky@gmail.com>

%post
    set -e
    pip install --no-cache-dir --root-user-action=ignore "{{ JAX }}" "/opt/jqscore[test]"
    find /opt/jqscore -name __pycache__ -prune -exec rm -rf {} +
    # What the image holds, for the record
    pip freeze > /opt/jqscore/pip-freeze.txt

%test
    cd /opt/jqscore && JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu python -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider tests

%runscript
    exec jqscore "$@"

%help
    jqscore: JAX-accelerated Q-score (atom-map fit of a model in a cryo-EM map).

    apptainer run --nv jqscore.sif STRUCTURE MAP [--sigma S] [--output TSV] [...]
        Q-scores of STRUCTURE (mmCIF or PDB) in MAP (MRC/CCP4); per-chain
        and per-residue summary, or a TSV with --output. --help lists the
        options.
    apptainer exec --nv jqscore.sif jqscore-cmd CHIMERA map=MAP cif=CIF [cif=CIF ...] [sigma=S]
        Drop-in for MapQ's mapq_cmd.py (as called by EMDB's VA): writes
        CIF__Q__MAP.cif with an _atom_site.Q-score column to the working
        directory. CHIMERA, np= and res= are accepted and ignored.
    apptainer exec jqscore.sif compare-qscores A.cif B.cif
        Per-atom differences of two such files.

    JAX takes 75% of the GPU's memory at start; to share the GPU, run with
    --env XLA_PYTHON_CLIENT_PREALLOCATE=false. --batch-size bounds the
    memory of the computation itself (the map is on the GPU throughout).
